   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% test threshold but removes any sales stop: exceeding it only triggers a corrective-action plan, so the Hearth 10 (6.2%) can keep selling. The recall trigger is set at 10 per 100,000 with no transition, and the 8-per-100,000 level only prompts notice and regulator review, so the Ember 8 (9.9) falls below the recall line. Reporting (24h/72h), the 36-month suppression start, and the 12-month new-unit and 6-year retrofit shut-off deadlines are within acceptable ranges."
 },
